Subject: [PATCH] feat: like/comment/share icons redesigned as a vertical stack
 near the price (item A.1)

Found and fixed a real, significant bug along the way: the like/save/
share buttons were only ever visible via CSS :hover (opacity:0 by
default, opacity:1 on .car-card:hover). This is a touch-based mobile
app - hover states don't reliably trigger on touch, so these buttons
were effectively unreachable on the actual product for most users.

Replaced the hover-only image overlay with an always-visible vertical
icon column positioned directly beside the price, as requested:
like (heart, with count), comment (speech bubble, with the new
commentCount), share, and save/favorite - each a compact icon+count
pair rather than the old wide text buttons ('LIKE 12', 'SAVE').

The comment icon has no separate handler - it's inside the card's
own Link, so tapping it (like tapping anywhere else on the card)
navigates to the car detail page where comments live, which is the
natural place to actually read/write them.

Also fixed the same hover-only bug for the one thing left in the old
overlay position (the admin-only delete button) - same reasoning,
admins need to actually be able to tap it on the mobile app.

Real layout bug caught and fixed before committing: my first pass
put the info block and the new action column as direct children of
car-info's flex-direction:column, which would have stacked them
vertically instead of side by side. Fixed by wrapping both in a row
container.
